From d641642eb57615580864ab2ad755216d67c40b5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:15:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire volume_efficiency (the volume x efficiency rebuild of
 dependent stats)

Built 2026-08 as a structural alternative to projecting yards, catches and TDs as their own per-game rates: project the opportunity
count first (attempts, carries, targets), then apply a per-opportunity efficiency shrunk by opportunities-of-evidence (K from the
published stabilization ranges: catch rate 50, yards per target 70, TD per target 120 ...) with a defense effect of numerator rating /
denominator rating. BUILT, MEASURED, REJECTED (methodology 'volume_efficiency'): +0.051 MAE, better in 5 of 26 weeks.
Removes the EFFICIENCY_RATIOS / EFFICIENCY_MATCHUP_CLIP / _shrunk_ratio / _efficiency_matchup section, the build block, the efficiency_*
keys of the explanation payload and one test. The UI's 'Efficiency rebuild' caption stays: it only shows when a saved explanation carries
the keys. _weighted_player_rates still returns its totals. Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
